Check out the PR head for issue https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102 and run `npm ci` at the repo root first. Create fixtures in a temp directory (`mktemp -d`), e.g.:
- `clean.jsonl` = `{"a":1}\n{"b":2}\n`
- `mid.jsonl` = `{"a":1}\n{bad\n{"c":3}\n`
- `torn.jsonl` = `{"a":1}\n{"b":` (printf, no trailing newline)
- `blank.jsonl` = `{"a":1}\n\n   \n{oops\n`

Check 1. Expect line: "packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file> prints <file>:<line>: <error> for every row that is not valid JSON (1-based lines, blank lines skipped, an unterminated last line checked) and exits 1 if any, 0 if none".
Run `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <fixture>; echo $?` for each fixture.
PASS when all of these hold:
- clean prints no error lines and exits 0.
- mid prints exactly one line that starts with `<fixture path as given>:2: ` followed by a non-empty error, and exits 1.
- torn prints a line starting `<path>:2: ` and exits 1.
- blank prints exactly one line starting `<path>:4: ` (no lines for 2 or 3) and exits 1.
- A file with two bad rows (e.g. `x\n{}\ny\n`) prints lines for 1 and 3 and exits 1.
FAIL if any line number, prefix or exit code differs, a blank line is reported, or the torn last row is missed.

Check 2. Expect line: "A missing file or no argument prints to stderr and exits 2".
Run `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js /nonexistent/x.jsonl` and `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js` (no argument), capturing stdout, stderr and the exit code separately.
PASS if both exit 2 with non-empty stderr. FAIL otherwise, including a crash with a different code.

Check 3. Expect line: "packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js exports lint(text) returning [{ line, error }]".
Run `node --input-type=module -e "import {lint} from './packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js'; console.log(JSON.stringify(lint('{}\n{bad\n'))); console.log(JSON.stringify(lint('{}\n')))"`.
PASS if `lint` is a named export, the first call returns an array with one object whose `line` is 2 and which has an `error` property, and the second returns `[]`. FAIL if the import fails, the export is missing, or the shape differs.

Check 4. Expect line: "The workspace has its own package.json (jsonl-lint, type module, test script node --test), no runtime dependencies, and node:test tests for a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn last row, blank lines and the exit codes".
Read `packages/jsonl-lint/package.json` with `node -e` and check `name === 'jsonl-lint'`, `type === 'module'`, `scripts.test === 'node --test'`, and that `dependencies` is absent or empty. Then run `npm test -w jsonl-lint` and inspect the test files.
PASS if:
- every package.json condition holds,
- the tests run with node:test and pass, and
- there are test cases covering each of: a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn last row, blank lines, and the exit codes.
FAIL if any field is wrong, there is any runtime dependency, any of the five scenarios has no test, or the tests fail.

Check 5. Expect line: "packages/jsonl-lint/README.md exists and the root README lists the tool".
Run `test -s packages/jsonl-lint/README.md` and `grep -n jsonl-lint README.md`.
PASS if the package README exists and is non-empty, and the root README mentions jsonl-lint as a tool. FAIL otherwise.

Check 6. Expect line: "The change is one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test whose body says Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102, and npm test and the test workflow are green at its head".
Run `gh pr view <pr> --repo suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test --json body,headRefOid,state`, `gh pr checks <pr> --repo suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test`, and at the checked-out head `npm ci && npm test; echo $?`.
PASS if:
- the PR exists on that repo,
- its body contains `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102`,
- local `npm test` exits 0 at the head commit, and
- the `test` workflow run for the head SHA concluded success.
FAIL if the body line is missing, local tests fail, the workflow failed or did not run for the head SHA, or the change is split across several PRs.

Advisory:
- Also check that `bin/jsonl-lint.js` has a node shebang and is executable, that CRLF input works, and that the root `README.md` no longer says there are no tools.
- These are not pass/fail conditions.